    "reasoning": "Mitigate 'H2 PCV Stuck Closed' (symptoms: PCV Command\u2013Actual Mismatch, Reactor Pressure High); keep temperatures, pressures and levels inside SIF limits and restore on-spec production. The brief's candidate levers are SET_SETPOINT (on the reactor pressure controller) and SET_THROUGHPUT (to adjust the plant load). The reactor is endothermic: lowering feed does NOT cool it. The plant load is always an operator lever. The fault 'H2 PCV Stuck Closed' affects the reactor pressure controller (R_PIC) and causes a mismatch between the PCV command and actual. The reactor pressure is high, which is a symptom of the fault. The reactor pressure controller is currently in AUTO mode with a setpoint of 4.0375 bar, which is above the alarm limit of 3.5 bar. Lowering the setpoint to 2.8 bar will bring it closer to the normal operating range. The throughput is currently 48.8769 kmol/h, which is below the lower bound of 0.0 kmol/h. Increasing the throughput to 90.0 kmol/h will help to relieve the load on the reactor.",
